  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Jifunze Uelewe (&#x201c;Learn to Understand&#x201d;)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tanzania):  With FY 2022 funds, USAID will reach approximately 1.25 million pre-primary through grade 4 pupils with interventions focused on improving literacy and numeracy skills in a safe and inclusive learning environment. The activity supports the GOT in institutionalizing phonics-based literacy instruction and  planning  and managing early grade literacy and numeracy interventions. USAID also aims to strengthen the social-emotional skills of more than 27,000 teachers, head teachers, and education officials. Using FY 2022 funds, USAID will: 1) train 17,113 teachers on incorporating Universal Design for Learning (UDL) principles in the instruction of literacy, numeracy and social and emotional skills; 2) provide virtual Continuous Professional Development (vCPD) to teachers in literacy, kiswahili, numeracy, inclusive education, and Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) to reinforce face-to-face training; 3) award Grants under Contracts (GUCs) to underutilized non- government organizations in target regions to work with local government authorities in the referral system for learners found with severe vision and hearing challenges; 4) replenish a complete set of grades 1-4 teaching and learning materials and conduct a learning assessment, the Decentralized Period Learning Assessment (DPLA), to measure progress in learning outcomes; and 5) revitalize Parent Teacher Partnerships (PTPs) and ensure they address school inclusion and school safety in their actions plans. ..This activity contributes $200,000 towards the Gender Based Violence (GBV) earmark of $400,000......</narrative>
  </description>
